<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jimmy Stevens</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–1994</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jimmy Stevens was a ni-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuatu">Vanuatu</a> political leader who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagriamel">Nagriamel</a> movement on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/espiritu-santo">Espiritu Santo</a> in the 1960s, campaigning for the return of land held by European planters. On the eve of independence in 1980 he led a secessionist rising on the island and declared the 'State of Vemerana'. The rising was put down with the help of troops from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>, and Stevens was imprisoned until 1991.</p></div>
